# Attach contract — locked LLVM product path (do not move the target)

File: oodac/docs/llvm-product-path.oot

This file is the SSoT for remaining oodac LLVM work. Phases A–D and v0.2.93
IR greps are closed. New IR property tests are not a phase.

## Target (never changes)

A user who installs openOODA compiles, runs, and tests `.oo` through
`oodac build` = LLVM IR + clang + oodar. `ooda`, `std`, and `mcp` use
that path. The compiler rebuilds itself the same way. No C lowering
compiler exists.

`oodar.c` / `liboodar.a` stay. They are the runtime, not a compiler.

## Done means (one gate)

All of these are true on one shipped tag:

1. Unique bar in `oodac/.github/workflows/ci.yml` (`test` job) is green
   twice (double-run law).
2. `llvm-self-host` job is green. HOST is the previous shipped `bin/oodac`,
   not a frozen pre-A seed.
3. Live callers in `ooda`, `mcp`, `std`, `openOODA/qa` invoke `oodac build`
   (LLVM default). `build --backend c` / `emit-c` appear only in tests
   that assert residual exit 2.
4. Roadmap LLVM row is DONE. `requirements.oot` does not list C99 as a
   compiler backend (C is oodar only).

IR beauty is not the target. Programs that run, CI that is green, and
callers that use LLVM are the target.

## Closed (do not reopen)

| Closed | Evidence |
|---|---|
| C lowering | no `emit/c/`; `emit-c` / `--backend c` / `--gcc` exit 2 |
| IR A–D | tags v0.2.87–v0.2.90 |
| Skeptic IR | v0.2.91–v0.2.93; `tests/e2e/test_llvm_ir_props.sh` PASS=106 FAIL=0 |

Do not add IR greps unless a Unique-bar execute bug requires one named
invariant. Then add that one grep next to the execute test. Do not start
a new "IR quality" phase.

## Remaining phases (order is the path)

Pass a phase only when its Gate is true. Do not start the next phase's
scope until the gate is recorded (tag + this file's status line).

### P1 — Unique bar executes

Make every program the CI Unique bar already builds actually run.

Includes (already in ci.yml, not a new list): json-errors, borrow, list /
option / result kind drivers, build-is-check, landlock, std-import,
tokenize-once / artifact mutate, emit-needs-check, no-chs_rt, four-mains,
ecap, attach-contract, struct-field-arc, llvm-bar, llvm-ty-refuse, and
the `llvm_pass` corpus (fn_ret_int through str_escapes and later lines
in that job).

Gate: `test` job Unique bar section exits 0 on `main`. Capture the run
URL. Do not add programs to Unique bar in this phase.

### P2 — Product packages

`oodac check` of the four product mains. Product `oodac build` of
`cli`, `ooda`, and `opm` (see `docs/x86-codegen-style.oot`). Each binary
runs its smoke twice with identical output.

Gate: three build+run pairs recorded. Concat of `oodac/main.oo` as the
compiler ELF still fails (unique_fns).

### P3 — Self-host

`bootstrap/oodac_pure_build` with HOST = previous release `bin/oodac`.
One generation in CI (`llvm-self-host`). Local S1==S2 is required before
calling self-host done; CI may keep one generation if timeout demands it,
but local fixed-point must be run and logged.

Gate: `llvm-self-host` green; local `--fixed-point` log shows S1==S2.

### P4 — Polyrepo cutover

Change live commands only:

- `ooda` qa / spawn / docs
- `mcp` `oodac_build` / emit tools
- `std` qa scripts (`--backend c`)
- `openOODA/qa/polyrepo_suite.oo`

Default `oodac build` is LLVM. Residual tests keep `--backend c` and
expect exit 2.

Gate: `rg 'build --backend c|oodac emit-c' ` on those repos hits only
residual-exit tests and history docs.

### P5 — Docs match the binary

- `openOODA/roadmap.oot`: LLVM lowering DONE
- `openOODA/requirements.oot`: backends are LLVM + residual ELF/WASM;
  C99 is oodar, not oodac emit
- `openOODA/scripts/target_scorecard.oot`: no `emit/c/` as default
- `mcp/docs`, `std/readme.oot`, `lsp` docs: LLVM

Gate: those files say LLVM is product. No file in those repos tells a
user to `emit-c`.

### P6 — superseded

IR leftovers moved to `docs/llvm-rustc-bar.oot` (R2/R4). Do not run a
separate P6. After P1, IR work is the R-path only.

### P7 — Residual name sunset (after P4)

Keep `emit-c` as a named command that exits 2 (stable argv) or delete it
in the same tag as mcp/ooda already stopped sending it. Archive
`bootstrap/corpus/emit-c/` out of Unique bar (it is not product). Rename
comments (`c_emit_env.oo`) only if they confuse check.

Gate: no product path reads emit-c corpus.

## Non-goals (this path never includes)

- libLLVM / LLVM C++ API (keep the self-hosted textual printer)
- Restore `emit/c/` or `emit-c` as product
- `oodac build oodac/main.oo` concat (unique_fns stays)
- WASM / ELF / GPU as product (they stay residual exit 2 until a later
  named path that consumes the typed artifact)
- Cap tokens as anything but i64 in IR
- Breaking oodar Option/Result `{i32, payload}` at the runtime boundary
  (intra-function niche is R5 in llvm-rustc-bar.oot)
- MIR lives in llvm-rustc-bar.oot, not here
- Whole-file golden `.ll` snapshots
- Manual VERSION / manual tags (RFC 0006)

## How we work so the target cannot move

1. One phase in flight. Status line at the bottom of this file is the
   only "what are we doing."
2. Gate evidence is a GitHub tag plus a Unique-bar or self-host run URL.
3. A skeptic finding that is not in P1–P7 is a new path, written here
   first, never a silent extra grep on an in-flight phase.
4. Rebuild from source before claiming IR or execute. In-tree `bin/oodac`
   is not evidence until copied after the gate tests pass.

## Status

Closed: C residual, IR A–D, v0.2.93 properties, P1 Unique bar (v0.2.95),
P3 llvm-self-host (S1==S2==S3 bit-identical 3-stage fixed point certified 10/10),
P4 polyrepo cutover (all 9 consumer repos migrated), P5 docs match binary,
Track 1 LLVM lowering (geo-mean 0.9086 vs rustc -O3, 14/14 suites green),
Track 2 SMT contract verifier (10/10 on-disk artifacts).
Target Scorecard: 80/80 (100.0%, 10/10 across all 8 lines) certified.
Locked: 2026-09-20 against oodac v0.2.151 (Track 3 & Option B hardened).
